---
import SiteShell from '../components/SiteShell.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
---

<SiteShell title="About Jay Yu" description="About Jay Yu, a Purdue computer science student, founder, and software builder.">
  <PageHeader
    label="README"
    title="About"
    description="I am a Purdue computer science student building useful software across backend systems, machine learning, robotics, and student products."
    meta={["Purdue CS", "LuntraHub", "ML and robotics"]}
  />

  <section class="dev-section">
    <div class="module-header">
      <div>
        <span class="module-label">PROFILE</span>
        <h2>README.md</h2>
      </div>
      <span class="status-chip">ACTIVE</span>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Hey, I am Jay.
        I study Computer Science at Purdue University and care about building technical systems that survive real use.
      </p>
      <p>
        My work spans Java, Python, React, Spring Boot, Node.js, PostgreSQL, TensorFlow, OpenCV, and robotics software.
        I like clean interfaces, strong feedback loops, reliable tests, and code that can be maintained after the first demo works.
      </p>
      <p>
        Recent work includes LoRA model refinement, vision-based robot localization, autonomous robotics sequences, real-time ASL translation, and LuntraHub, a student connection and tutor discovery platform.
      </p>
      <h2>Operating principles</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Prototype quickly, then simplify the system until the important parts are obvious.</li>
        <li>Measure real behavior, not just local happy paths.</li>
        <li>Use the smallest architecture that can stay reliable as the product grows.</li>
        <li>Keep learning from research, production constraints, and users in the loop.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Now</h2>
      <p>
        I am focused on Purdue CS, LuntraHub, ML and robotics projects, and publishing technical notes from the systems I am building.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteShell>
